# Declarative map of every credential the protected release lanes need.
#
# FORMAT (whitespace separated, four columns):
#   <github-environment>  <secret-name>  <1password-reference>  <required|optional>
#
# The 1Password reference is an `op://<vault>/<item>/<field>` secret reference.
# Run `./tooling/provision-release-secrets.sh --discover` to have candidate
# references filled in for you from the titles of items in your own vaults; it
# never reads a value during discovery and never touches the Squad vault.
#
# NOTHING IN THIS FILE IS A SECRET. It names where secrets live, not what they
# are. It is committed deliberately so the credential surface is reviewable.

recovery-protected  KEEPLING_BACKUP_PRIMARY_ENDPOINT    op://Personal/Keepling backup primary/endpoint    required
recovery-protected  KEEPLING_BACKUP_PRIMARY_REGION      op://Personal/Keepling backup primary/region      required
recovery-protected  KEEPLING_BACKUP_PRIMARY_ACCESS_KEY  op://Personal/Keepling backup primary/access key id      required
recovery-protected  KEEPLING_BACKUP_PRIMARY_SECRET_KEY  op://Personal/Keepling backup primary/secret access key   required

recovery-live       HCLOUD_TOKEN                        op://Personal/Hetzner Cloud/api token             required
recovery-live       CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN                op://Personal/Cloudflare/api token                required
recovery-live       KEEPLING_DNS_ZONE_ID                op://Personal/Cloudflare/zone id                  required
recovery-live       KEEPLING_DNS_RECORD_NAME            op://Personal/Cloudflare/record name              required
